-- ============================================================================
-- ALL DAY — the eight apps' new boards. One small paste.
--
-- Project:  jnouvwxomrcffqwilqkq (the fleet's one shared project)
-- Prefix:   nn_
-- Written:  2026-10-29 (wave 0 of the eight apps)
-- Needs:    nn-SETUP.sql, nn-ROUND2.sql, nn-ROUND3.sql, nn-ROUND4.sql and
--           nn-PLAYLISTS.sql, already pasted (they are).
--
-- How to run: Supabase dashboard -> SQL Editor -> New query -> paste this
-- WHOLE file -> Run. Safe to run again. (all-day/supabase/SETUP-APPS.md
-- says the same in four lines.)
--
-- What it does, in plain words: it replaces one function, nn_rules(), with
-- the same rules plus seven new boards and their twelve kinds of post:
--   nightlife  open_tonight                    Out: "my group is out tonight"
--   sports     session                         Out and Body: pickup, a workout
--   stage      logged                          Out: a show you saw
--   neighbors  borrow, free, favor, lost, found People: the Neighbor Exchange
--   shifts     shift                           People: volunteer slots (Stephen looks first)
--   clubs      idea                            People: start a club
--   streets    report                          Town: potholes, streetlights (Stephen looks first)
--   rescue     rescue                          Eat: food left at closing
-- Nothing else changes: no table, column, row, policy or grant is touched.
-- The existing functions read every board from nn_rules(), and already check
-- each field's type, a post's lifetime, a link (only on a board Stephen
-- approves first), the photo queue and the posting limits, so the new boards
-- get the old moderation (reports, the boards desk in mod.html) as they are.
-- No tab posts to them yet; the app sessions of wave 1 and 2 build those.
--
-- The rules stay at version 3 (nothing was taken away and no field type is
-- new). This is the same JSON as RULES in all-day/js/boards-core.js and as
-- the copies in nn-ROUND4.sql and nn-PLAYLISTS.sql;
-- scripts/test-boards-core.mjs fails if any two differ. Undo: paste
-- nn-PLAYLISTS.sql from before 2026-10-29 (the new boards' posts, if any,
-- stay in the table, unlisted).
-- ============================================================================

